Project Information
📌 Project Overview

ResumeIQ is a full-stack web application that integrates modern web development with AI-assisted resume analysis and career guidance.

The application allows users to upload resumes, extract important information, compare their resumes with job descriptions, identify relevant skills, review potential skill gaps, and receive personalized career recommendations.

Unlike a static resume-checking interface, the intended application uses a backend API and relational database to manage user accounts, resumes, analysis history, recommendations, chatbot conversations, and support requests.

The platform also includes an administrator interface for managing users, support tickets, frequently asked questions, and operational analytics.

The Problem

Many job seekers struggle to understand how effectively their resumes communicate their qualifications in relation to a particular job.

Common challenges include:

Difficulty identifying relevant skills in a resume.
Uncertainty about whether a resume addresses a job description.
Missing or insufficiently demonstrated requirements.
Difficulty choosing suitable career paths.
Lack of clear and actionable resume improvement suggestions.
Limited visibility into previous resume analyses.
The Solution

ResumeIQ provides a centralized platform that helps users:

Analyze resume content automatically.
Compare resumes against job descriptions.
Identify matching skills and keywords.
Find requirements that are not clearly demonstrated.
Explore relevant career categories.
Review personalized learning suggestions.
Save and revisit previous analyses.
Access career guidance through a chatbot.
Contact support through a ticket-management system.
🎯 Project Objectives

The main objectives of ResumeIQ are:

Develop a complete full-stack web application using React and FastAPI.
Implement an NLP pipeline for extracting useful information from resumes.
Calculate resume and job-description text similarity using TF-IDF and cosine similarity.
Identify skills and compare them with job requirements.
Recommend relevant career categories using explainable analysis.
Provide useful resume improvement suggestions.
Implement secure authentication and role-based authorization.
Store application data in PostgreSQL.
Develop a responsive user dashboard and administrator dashboard.
Build a chatbot with predefined career-related questions and answers.
Provide a searchable Help Center and support ticket system.
Demonstrate practical AI, machine learning, database, API, and cybersecurity concepts.
✨ Key Features
1. AI-Powered Resume Analyzer

ResumeIQ analyzes uploaded resumes and extracts useful information.

Supported formats:

PDF
DOCX
TXT

Features:

Drag-and-drop file upload.
File validation and processing status.
Resume text extraction.
Resume section identification.
Skill extraction.
Education and experience information extraction where supported.
Resume strengths and improvement suggestions.
Persistent analysis history.
Clear processing errors when a document cannot be analyzed.

Users can review the extracted information and correct mistakes where editing functionality is available.

2. Job Description Matcher

The Job Description Matcher compares a selected resume with a job description.

It provides:

Text-similarity score.
Matching skills.
Missing or insufficiently demonstrated requirements.
Relevant resume evidence where available.
Keyword alignment.
Suggested resume improvements.
Saved comparison results.

Users can compare the same resume against multiple job descriptions.

Note: A skill missing from a resume is not necessarily a skill the candidate lacks. It may simply be absent from the document or insufficiently demonstrated.

3. Skill Extraction

The platform uses a configurable skill taxonomy to identify skills in resume text.

Skill categories include:

Programming Languages.
Web Development.
Data Science.
Machine Learning.
Cloud Computing.
Databases.
Cybersecurity.
Project Management.
Communication.
Problem Solving.

The extraction pipeline is designed to preserve important technical expressions such as C++, C#, .NET, and Node.js.

4. Career Recommendations

ResumeIQ recommends potential career categories based on extracted skills, resume information, and user preferences.

Each recommendation can include:

Job title.
Explanation of relevance.
Relevant skills.
Skills to develop.
Suggested learning resources.
Recommended next steps.

Users can save recommendations and update their status where supported.

Career recommendations are intended to support exploration, not make employment decisions on behalf of users.

5. Resume Improvement Suggestions

The platform can provide practical suggestions to improve resume clarity and relevance.

Examples include:

Using clearer section headings.
Improving professional summaries.
Rewriting vague bullet points.
Highlighting relevant projects.
Using specific examples of achievements.
Aligning resume language with job requirements.
Identifying skills that need stronger evidence.

Optional generative AI integration can provide more advanced writing suggestions.

Generated content must be reviewed by the user and must not invent qualifications, certifications, employment history, or achievements.

6. User Dashboard

The dashboard provides a centralized view of the user's career-analysis activity.

It can display:

Total resume analyses.
Latest similarity score.
Saved career recommendations.
Recent analysis history.
Skills overview.
Analysis activity charts.
Recent support tickets.
Quick navigation to important features.

All dashboard metrics should come from actual application records rather than fabricated production data.

7. Analysis History

Authenticated users can revisit saved analyses.

The history section can include:

Resume information.
Job title or target role.
Text-similarity score.
Analysis date.
Extracted skills.
Matching requirements.
Suggested improvements.

Users must only be able to access their own records.

8. AI Career Assistant

ResumeIQ includes a chatbot named ResumeIQ AI Career Assistant.

The chatbot provides predefined answers to ten common career questions and can optionally support an LLM-powered mode.

Features include:

Suggested questions.
Basic keyword-based matching.
Chat message history.
Loading and error states.
Helpful fallback responses.
Navigation to the Help Center.
Clear chat-history controls.
Optional generative AI integration.

The predefined FAQ functionality must work without a paid AI service.

9. Help Center

The Help Center provides information about using the platform.

It includes:

Searchable FAQs.
Help article categories.
Getting Started guidance.
Account management assistance.
Resume-analysis guidance.
Career-development information.
Privacy information.
Contact Support functionality.
10. Support Ticket System

Users can submit support requests and track their progress.

A support ticket can include:

Ticket ID.
Subject.
Category.
Description.
Priority.
Status.
Creation date.
Last-updated date.
Conversation messages.
Assigned administrator, where applicable.

Supported ticket statuses:

OPEN
IN_PROGRESS
WAITING_FOR_USER
RESOLVED
CLOSED

Users must only be able to access their own tickets. Administrators can manage tickets according to their permissions.

11. Admin Dashboard

The administrator interface provides authorized access to application-management functions.

Features include:

Registered-user statistics.
Resume-analysis statistics.
Recent registrations.
Open support tickets.
Analysis activity charts.
Job-category statistics.
User account management.
Support ticket management.
FAQ management.
System activity logs.
Administrative audit trails.

All administrative endpoints must enforce authorization on the backend.

12. Responsive Design

ResumeIQ is designed for different screen sizes.

Supported target devices include:

Android phones.
iPhones.
iPads.
Android tablets.
Laptops.
Desktop computers.

The interface uses responsive layouts, accessible forms, touch-friendly controls, and mobile-friendly navigation.

13. Optional Generative AI and RAG

Optional AI integrations can enhance the core NLP pipeline.

Potential capabilities include:

Resume bullet-point rewriting.
Professional-summary improvement.
Skill-gap explanations.
Personalized learning plans.
Career guidance based on trusted reference material.

Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) can retrieve relevant career-guidance documents and provide source-grounded answers.

The core analysis pipeline should continue working when an optional external LLM provider is unavailable.

