💻 Installation and Setup

Follow these instructions to prepare a local development environment.

Prerequisites

Install:

Git.
Node.js and npm.
Python 3.11 or a compatible version supported by the pinned dependencies.
PostgreSQL.
Visual Studio Code or another code editor.

Docker and Docker Compose may be used if the repository includes a working Docker configuration.

Step 1: Clone the Repository

Replace the placeholder with your actual GitHub repository URL.

git clone <YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL>
cd RESUMEIQ
Step 2: Set Up the Backend

Move into the backend directory:

cd backend

Create a Python virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv

Activate the environment.

Windows PowerShell:

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

Windows Command Prompt:

.venv\Scripts\activate.bat

macOS or Linux:

source .venv/bin/activate

Install the backend dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt
Step 3: Configure the Backend Environment

Create a local environment file from the example:

Windows PowerShell:

Copy-Item .env.example .env

macOS or Linux:

cp .env.example .env

Update the environment variables with your local database connection and security settings.

Never commit the real .env file.

Step 4: Configure PostgreSQL

Create a PostgreSQL database and a dedicated application user.

For example, using the PostgreSQL command-line client:

CREATE USER resumeiq_user WITH PASSWORD 'replace_with_a_strong_password';
CREATE DATABASE resumeiq OWNER resumeiq_user;

Use a secure password and configure access according to your local PostgreSQL setup.

Update DATABASE_URL in the backend environment file.

Example:

DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://resumeiq_user:replace_with_a_strong_password@localhost:5432/resumeiq

Ensure the PostgreSQL driver required by the application is installed.

Step 5: Run Database Migrations

From the backend directory, run:

alembic upgrade head

This command applies the migrations defined by the project.

If migrations have not yet been created or configured, complete that setup before relying on database persistence.

Step 6: Start the Backend Server

From the backend directory:

uvicorn app.main:app --reload

The example assumes the FastAPI application is exposed as app in backend/app/main.py.

If the actual entry point differs, adjust the command accordingly.

The local API is typically available at:

http://127.0.0.1:8000

Step 7: Set Up the Frontend

Open a second terminal from the repository root:

cd frontend

Install frontend dependencies:

npm install

Create a frontend environment file:

Windows PowerShell:

Copy-Item .env.example .env

macOS or Linux:

cp .env.example .env

Configure the API base URL:

VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1

Ensure this variable name matches the frontend's API-client configuration.

Step 8: Start the Frontend

Run:

npm run dev

Vite will display the development URL in the terminal, commonly:

http://localhost:5173

Open the displayed URL in your browser.

Step 9: Verify the Application

Confirm that:

The frontend opens successfully.
The backend starts without errors.
PostgreSQL is accessible.
Database migrations have completed.
Registration and login work.
The frontend can call the backend.
Resume upload and analysis return real results.
Analysis records persist after reloading the page.

These steps are general setup instructions and must be checked against the actual project files.

🔧 Environment Configuration

The application should use environment variables for database credentials, security settings, file storage, email, and optional external services.

Example Backend Environment
APP_ENV=development
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://resumeiq_user:change_me@localhost:5432/resumeiq

SECRET_KEY=replace_with_a_long_random_secret

ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=15
REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS=7

FRONTEND_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

UPLOAD_DIR=./private_uploads
MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE_MB=10

SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USERNAME=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
EMAIL_FROM=

LLM_PROVIDER=
LLM_API_KEY=
Example Frontend Environment
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1

Security notes:

These names are examples; use the variables actually supported by your code.
Generate strong, unique application secrets.
Do not commit credentials or real environment files.
Never expose private backend secrets through frontend environment variables.
Configure secure cookies, HTTPS, and trusted CORS origins for production.
Keep optional LLM configuration separate from the core NLP pipeline.
🤖 Chatbot and Help Center

The ResumeIQ AI Career Assistant includes ten predefined questions.

Q1. How can I improve my resume?

Use clear headings, concise bullet points, relevant skills, and specific examples of your achievements. Tailor your resume to the requirements of each job.

Q2. What skills are in demand right now?

Relevant skills depend on your target role and location. Technical areas such as data analysis, software development, cloud computing, and cybersecurity can be useful starting points. Check current job descriptions to identify the skills employers are requesting.

Q3. Which jobs are best for my profile?

ResumeIQ can suggest relevant job categories based on the skills and experience identified in your resume. Review the recommendations and select roles that match your interests and goals.

Q4. How can I prepare for an interview?

Research the employer, review the job description, practice explaining your projects, prepare examples of your achievements, and rehearse common technical and behavioral questions.

Q5. What is a good salary for my experience?

Salary depends on your location, industry, experience, and employer. Compare current job postings and reputable salary surveys for your target role.

Q6. Can you help me write a cover letter?

Yes. Provide the job description and details about your relevant experience. ResumeIQ can help draft a tailored cover letter that accurately represents your background.

Q7. How do I switch careers?

Identify transferable skills, research your target role, compare your current skills with its requirements, and build relevant projects or qualifications to address important gaps.

Q8. What are the top companies hiring?

Hiring activity changes over time and location. Check current employer career pages and reputable job boards to find opportunities relevant to your skills.

Q9. How can I improve my LinkedIn profile?

Use a clear professional headline, write a concise summary, highlight relevant projects and accomplishments, and keep your skills and experience up to date.

Q10. Can you suggest learning resources?

Start with resources aligned with your target role. Consider official documentation, structured online courses, practical projects, and reputable educational platforms.

Chatbot Behavior

The predefined chatbot should:

Display suggested questions.
Return the associated answer when a question is selected.
Support basic keyword-based matching.
Provide a helpful fallback for unrecognized questions.
Link users to relevant Help Center resources.
Respect chat-retention settings.
Allow users to clear their chat history.

An optional LLM mode may extend the chatbot, but the predefined FAQ system must work without a paid API.

